	\bALLIES:\B
	None
	
	\bENEMIES:\B
	None
	
	Zoners are a diverse group of individuals who, for various reasons, have decided to live in the wild and unregulated systems outside of colonial control.

H 66220
	The Tanner Belt entirely engulfs the Bering System. Despite intensive surveys by both Liberty and Rheinland mining corporations, no mineral deposits of economic value have ever been discovered within the barren rock asteroids of the vast field. Unioners and Xenos have been spotted within the system regularly.

H 66221
	\b\cr>>>WARNING: NAVIGATIONAL HAZARD<<<\B\C
	
	The Omega-7 region of the Walker Nebula is rich in mineral resources. Explosive gas pockets are scattered through the cloud, making any travel away from Trade Lanes and known mining areas hazardous. Only recently settled, its rich deposits of Cobalt, Silver, and Copper are being exploited by the IMG, Daumann, and Krüger.

H 66222
	\b\cr>>>WARNING: NAVIGATIONAL HAZARD<<<\B\C
	
	The Omicron-Beta Edge Nebula is rich in Alien Organisms, present on the surface of most asteroids. Its high background radiation levels do not invite lingering, however. Exposure time in open space should be minimized. Due to the very high pirate activity in this system, caution is advised at all times.

H 66223
	\b\cr>>>WARNING: NAVIGATIONAL HAZARD<<<\B\C
	
	The Sigma-13 region of the Crow Nebula is rich in ionized Hydrogen, Helium, and Oxygen. Home territory of the GMG, the cloud contains the debris field remnants of the once-proud Rheinland Imperial fleet. Travel off of marked Trade Lanes is hazardous and not recommended due to numerous explosive Oxygen gas pockets. Pirate activity is also quite high throughout the cloud.

H 66224
	A large rock asteroid field containing rich deposits of Niobium and Beryllium, it is the focus of Border World mining operations by both the IMG and BMM. Outcast activity is very high in the system, leading authorities to believe that it is astride a key Outcast smuggling route.

H 66225
	A vast field of water ice with some oxygen ice pockets. The Tau-31 field lies in the heart of the Barrier. The Planetform terraforming project is the most notable activity in the system, along with the Holman outpost, a key supply depot for the IMG and its operations further afield in Tau-23. A Trade Lane is currently under construction between Holman and the Tau-23 Gate, but its completion has been delayed by recent pirate attacks.

H 66226
	\b\cr>>>WARNING: HIGH RADIATION AREA<<<\B\C
	
	The Omega-41 fragment field is all that remains of the system’s planets following the planetary nova which occurred shortly before the arrival of humans in the Sirius Sector.

H 66227
	CLASS: Unknown
	CREW: Unknown
	ARMAMENT: Unknown
	
	The Osiris is the command ship for The Order. Its advanced technology — including stealth capability — has led to speculation that it was originally a Liberty military prototype before being stolen by the mysterious Orillion, leader of The Order.

H 66228
	DIAMETER: 13,100 km
	MASS: 6.72 x 10\f09²\4\F kg
	TERRAIN: Ice
	TEMPERATURE: -50°C to -10°C
	ESCAPE VELOCITY: 10.02 km/s
	
	The frozen planet of Atka was once targeted to be terraformed by the Liberty government in an attempt to relocate manufacturing and economic undesirables to the Independent Worlds. That plan is currently on hold until the system can be made more secure for commerce.

H 66229
	DIAMETER: 4,972 km
	MASS: 3.0 x 10\f09²\4\F kg
	TERRAIN: Volcanic
	TEMPERATURE: 300°C to 500°C
	ESCAPE VELOCITY: 6.75 km/s
	
	Named after the senior lieutenant on Von Rohe’s fateful expedition, Schutz is a dying planet, slowly being melted by the swelling red giant sun at the system’s center. One of only two planets still intact in the system, its surface is convulsed by numerous volcanos. It serves as a shield for the Solarius Station, protecting it from the intense radiation emitted by the dying sun.

H 66230
	DIAMETER: 19,450 km
	MASS: 10.04 x 10\f09²\4\F kg
	TERRAIN: N/A
	TEMPERATURE: N/A
	ESCAPE VELOCITY: 17.02 km/s
	
	Little is known about the frozen gas giant Mallorca. Mostly likely composition is frozen methane mixed with unknown trace gases.

H 66231
	DIAMETER: 25,412 km
	MASS: 13.04 x 10\f09²\4\F kg
	TERRAIN: N/A
	TEMPERATURE: N/A
	ESCAPE VELOCITY: 18.02 km/s
	
	The gas giant Seto consists primarily of hydrogen. Its striking orange color and location astride the primary Liberty-Kusari trade route make it a memorable landmark. Its only moon, Junyo, is the sole habitable planet within the Shikoku System.

H 66399
	Probable remains of the \iTrujillo\I, a Corsair ship smuggling Artifacts into New London.

H 66400
	The Molly fighter \iVanguard\I, identified and pursued by Bretonia Armed Forces fighters several weeks ago. Could be carrying Gold.

H 66401
	The wreck of the Outcast fighter \iPuno\I, missing since 751. Most likely contains a cargo of Cardamine.

H 66402
	The wreck of the \iHenry Jones\I  armored transport, a Bowex ship that was hijacked by Corsairs several weeks ago. It was transporting a shipment of Gold to Rheinland.

H 66403
	The Corsair ship \iCaraz\I, intercepted and pursued by an Armed Forces patrol several weeks ago. May contain Artifacts.

H 66404
	The remains of the \iSan Vicente\I, an Outcast Cardamine smuggler, which was intercepted and destroyed by an Armed Forces patrol several weeks ago.

H 66405
	The remains of the lost Outcast ship \iLorenzo\I, caught by the military and pursued into this radioactive area. Its Cardamine cargo has not been recovered.

H 66406
	An escort of the \iStorm\I, a Bretonian gunboat that hit a mine and exploded while chasing rebels in the Founders Day Revolt of 752.

H 66407
	The wreck of the Molly fighter \iScargill\I, destroyed by BMM security forces after it was caught trespassing on GS&M property.

H 66408
	A dead Corsair warrior’s ship. There are many of these scattered throughout the Omega-5 battlefield, especially in the vicinity of the Hammen Hole.

H 66409
	One of many Red Hessian fighter wrecks in this battlefield. Most of them are picked clean, but some yield weapons.

H 66410
	The wreck of the Republican freight train \iBremerhaven\I. It was carrying a cargo of Engine Components bound for Southampton.

H 66411
	The wreck of the \iMonschau\I, a Krüger Silver freighter that was attacked by Hessians.

H 66412
	Remnants of an early Corsair raiding party, in the Omega-7 System, that blundered into this gas pocket.

H 66413
	The remains of a Bounty Hunter. The Hunter may have been stalking Red Hessians, but more likely just looking for Diamonds.

H 66414
	The remains of a Corsair fighter. They often come in from Omega-41 for a little raiding and Diamond mining.

H 66415
	The wreckage of a Daumann company ship. Most likely an employee trying to find some Diamonds to sell on their own.

H 66416
	The remnants of a Red Hessian fighter. The pirates in the area often come here looking for Diamonds.

H 66417
	The Krüger gas mining area was abandoned early on in the Eighty Years’ War, almost overnight. In their haste to depart, the Krüger personnel left several cargo pods intact. As far as anyone knows, they are still out there, scattered among the debris. The south oxygen pocket has since drifted over the site, making recovery a difficult proposition at best.

H 66418
	Wreckage of one of the escorts of the \iKassel\I, a Rheinland Heavy Cruiser that was destroyed during the Eighty Years’ War.

H 66419
	Destroyed Rheinland Imperial Fleet fighter from the Eighty Years’ War. This one was lost in the Battle of the Yanagi Cloud.

H 66420
	The wreck of the \iMongoose\I, a ship flown by the Bounty Hunter named Jim Adams. He disappeared shortly after the Freeport disaster.

H 66421
	The wreck of the \iRobert Fitzgerald\I, a Cryer freighter that was attacked by Outcasts some weeks ago. It was hauling Alien Organisms to Atka for research purposes.

H 66422
	The remains of the \iMenorca\I. The Corsair ship was lost in a recent skirmish with Outcasts. It is believed to be carrying Artifacts.

H 66423
	The wreck of the \iHien\I, the ship of a famous GMG ace. Most likely the work of Outcasts.

H 66424
	The wreck of the \iPerez\I, the ship of an Outcast Cardamine smuggler. The GMG claims responsibility.

H 66425
	The wreck of the \iWolverine\I, flown by Bounty Hunter Ryan McKeen, left as a warning to others who venture too close to Outcast bases.

H 66426
	The wreck of the hijacked freight train \iEdmund Marshall\I. It was later disabled by a BMM patrol. Its cargo was Beryllium.

H 66427
	The wreck of the DSE freighter \iWhetstone\I, which carried Construction Machinery. Most likely the work of Outcasts.

H 66428
	Wreckage of the \iValiant\I, a Gaian fighter flown by Lucy Collins.

H 66429
	The remains of the \iGriffin\I. The registered owner was the Bounty Hunter Jessica Stephenson.

H 66430
	The wreckage of the IMG freighter \iBarossa\I. The ship was attacked by Outcasts several months ago. It was carrying Niobium.

H 66431
	The wreck of the \iPathfinder\I. Its pilot, “T-Bob” Biggs, was a Bounty Hunters Guild ace. There should be good equipment available.

H 66432
	The wreck of the \iHosho Maru\I, a GMG exploratory vessel in search of H-Fuel.

H 66433
	One of the GMG escorts of the \iHosho Maru\I. The expedition was in search of new H-Fuel deposits when they were set upon by unknown assailants.

H 66434
	The remains of the IMG freighter \iIndependence\I. The ship is part of the failed IMG effort to establish Diamond mining operations in Omega-41.

H 66435
	The wreck of the Red Hessian fighter \iVolsung\I. The ship belonged to an elite pilot.

H 66436
	The remains of the \iRebel\I. This ship was flown by a Corsair turncoat named Jesse Casas, who joined the Bounty Hunters.

H 66437
	The wreck of the \iFearless\I, a Bretonian research vessel lost in 550. It may contain Artifacts.

H 66438
	The wreckage of the \iViking\I, flown by Bounty Hunter Kelly Nielson.

H 66439
	An Outcast tomb. This ship contains the deceased pilot and his most prized possessions.

H 66440
	The wreck of the Bounty Hunter fighter \iVengeance\I. This ship was flown by “Lucky” Logan Conner, who stretched his luck a little too far.

H 66441
	This ship is part of the Graveyard of the Innocents, where young Corsairs must prove their worthiness or perish in the process. Many of these ships contain Artifacts.

H 66442
	Remnants of a Xeno fighter. It was probably destroyed by the Unioners, who have no use for Xeno weapons.

H 66443
	The Universal Shipping transport \iBradley\I. It was reported missing yesterday. The cargo manifest lists Trade Lane Parts.

H 66444
	The wreck of the \iEdward Kane\I, a Bowex armored transport carrying Gold. Hijacked recently by Rogues.

H 66445
	The Universal large transport \iMcKinley\I, hauling Superconductors. This is one of three known ships that were destroyed in 784 by a dark matter storm.

H 66446
	The wreck of the \iKamakura Maru\I, a Samura transport carrying Niobium that was lost in the Dark Matter Storm of 784.

H 66447
	Wreckage of the Samura armored transport \iNikko Maru\I. It was carrying Luxury Goods from New York to New Tokyo when it was caught in the Dark Matter Storm of 784.

H 66448
	The Universal Shipping transport \iChesapeake\I  was hijacked several months ago. It may still have Pharmaceuticals aboard.

H 66449
	Remains of the \iFreespirit\I, the ship of a Rogue Artifact smuggler. It was lost after a Bounty Hunter ambush.

H 66450
	The remains of the \iShibuya Maru\I. The Golden C. ship was making a Cardamine run to Galileo when it was intercepted by a Bounty Hunter.

H 66451
	The wreck of the \iKobe Maru\I. The Hogosha used this ship as an Artifact smuggler. It disappeared some time ago.

H 66452
	The Blood Dragon fighter \iShoki\I. This is the patrol leader’s ship that has been missing since a battle with Kusari Naval Forces.

H 66453
	The remnants of the \iOhtori\I, an escort to the Golden C. ship \iYukari Maru\I. The ship was intercepted by a Kusari Naval Forces patrol while crossing the Kyushu System.

H 66454
	The wreck of the Blood Dragon assault fighter \iFugaku\I. It was lost during a raid on the Kansai Research Center.

H 66455
	The remains of the Corsair fighter \iMalaga\I, recently lost in an encounter with the GMG.

H 66456
	The wreck of the \iJames Morrell\I. The DSE ship was transporting Trade Lane Parts to the Chugoku Gate Construction Site when it was attacked by Blood Dragons.

H 66457
	A destroyed Kusari Naval Forces fighter. One of many unretrieved military ships in the Kayo Cloud.

H 66458
	The wreckage of the \iAggressor\I, the ship of infamous Bounty Hunter, Harry Riggs.

H 66459
	Probable remains of missing Liberty Navy Patrol 27.

H 66460
	Wreckage of the Rogue Fighter \iFlint\I, which has been missing for several weeks. There may be Cardamine cargo aboard.

H 66461
	The wreck of the Outcast ship \iBalboa\I. It was identified and pursued by LPI forces several weeks ago. There may be Cardamine in the hold.

H 66462
	The wreckage of the \iAvenger\I, piloted by Bounty Hunter Annie “Shorty” Davis.

H 66463
	An older model of the C-class utility transport, probably the remains of the supply ship \iFt. Worth\I, which was lost in the Dallas Incident in 521. It was carrying a load of Trade Lane Parts.

H 66464
	The remains of the Dallas Research Station Superconductor Laboratory, which was destroyed in 521 AS after a failed Jump Gate experiment.

H 66465
	The remains of the Rogue fighter \iPrudhoe\I, which disappeared during a Diamond smuggling run.

H 66466
	The remains of a Red Hessian fighter, probably trapped by the radiation in the area.

H 66467
	A destroyed Unioner ship. Most likely cause is radiation. There may be Diamonds aboard.

H 66468
	The wreck of the \iBabylon\I. The Orbital Spa ship was attacked by the LWB along the Trade Lane to Baden-Baden some time ago. It was carrying Luxury Goods.

H 66469
	The hulk of the Synth Foods ship \iBelknap\I. This ship was just reported lost by Synth Foods a few days ago. It may still contain Luxury Food cargo.

H 66470
	The remains of the Red Hessian ship \iNurnberg\I. It is believed that they were running Side Arms out to bases in the Border Worlds.

H 66471
	One of the lost ships of Rheinland Federal Police Patrol 421, which disappeared several months ago.

H 66472
	Scanning reveals older Rheinland Freighter model. The most likely candidate is the \iDanzig\I, a Krüger Minerals ship lost in 450. It may be carrying Diamonds.

H 66489
	A mooring fixture is a temporary resting area for idle ships within the active shipping zone near planets.

